< From September 27 to October 1, 2026, the 14.2 refinement work ran the preregistered studies PREREG16 to PREREG37 (with PREREG28b) against the 14.1 benchmark record. **No engine file, coefficient or default of the shipped 14.1 was changed by any of them, and 14.1 remains the release.** The work produced an adopted scoring convention (volume under C1, or C2 where tags allow), an adopted scorer revision (r2, from PREREG37 on), one regional NS candidate that passes its benchmark gates but has not cleared a Bakuzis grid (v141LTfi), and named failures that locate the remaining NS and QC errors. These notes treat the QC height anchor as open, because PREREG37 found that the tag pairs behind the size dependent QC anchor were formed by row index. Each gated verdict follows a decision rule fixed before any held out value was read, and the one post hoc step, the PREREG21 split of its survivor term, is declared as such in that RESULT.
---
> From September 27 to October 2, 2026, the 14.2 refinement work ran the preregistered studies PREREG16 to PREREG42 (with PREREG28b) against the 14.1 benchmark record. **No engine file, coefficient or default of the shipped 14.1 was changed by any of them, and 14.1 remains the release.** The work produced an adopted scoring convention (volume under C1, or C2 where tags allow), an adopted scorer revision (r2, from PREREG37 on), one regional NS candidate that passes its benchmark gates but has not cleared a Bakuzis grid (v141LTfi), and named failures that locate the remaining NS and QC errors. The QC height anchor track is closed with the shipped 0.111 kept for 14.2: a field tag anchor (1.242) corrects QC height growth on the benchmark but does not clear the Bakuzis QC grid (PREREG38 to PREREG41), and the earlier QC height gates built on row index pairs are corrected by an erratum (PREREG42). Each gated verdict follows a decision rule fixed before any held out value was read, and the one post hoc step, the PREREG21 split of its survivor term, is declared as such in that RESULT.
43c43
< PREREG19 scored QC_AFAC from 0.030 to 1.000 under C1. The screened qc_c fold A C1 ratio spanned only 0.0067 across the grid, below the 0.010 threshold, so the anchor is a height calibration and the QC volume excess sits in diameters and stems (stems about 24% low on fold B at every anchor). These notes use revision 2 of that RESULT, which withdraws its C2 numbers. PREREG23 refit the anchor on tag height increment. On its tagged survivors the shipped 0.111 predicted about a tenth of observed increment (fold B pooled ratio 0.086), and the candidate 1.061 lifted the ratio to 0.828 but moved the 25 cm and over class from -0.021 to +0.099 m yr⁻¹, worse by 0.077. PREREG37 later showed that these survivors, like those of PREREG28 and PREREG28b, were paired on row index frames. PREREG24 was a QC stems and QMD diagnostic, and its RESULT is not on the host, so neither its verdict nor its numbers is cited.
---
> PREREG19 scored QC_AFAC from 0.030 to 1.000 under C1. The screened qc_c fold A C1 ratio spanned only 0.0067 across the grid, below the 0.010 threshold, so the anchor is a height calibration and the QC volume excess sits in diameters and stems (stems about 24% low on fold B at every anchor). These notes use revision 2 of that RESULT, which withdraws its C2 numbers. PREREG23 refit the anchor on tag height increment. On its tagged survivors the shipped 0.111 predicted about a tenth of observed increment (fold B pooled ratio 0.086), and the candidate 1.061 lifted the ratio to 0.828 but moved the 25 cm and over class from -0.021 to +0.099 m yr⁻¹, worse by 0.077. PREREG37 later showed that these survivors, like those of PREREG28 and PREREG28b, were paired on row index frames, and under field tags the PREREG42 erratum reverses this verdict: the 25 cm and over class is better than 0.111 by 0.108 m yr⁻¹ and every gate as PREREG23 coded it passes. PREREG24 was a QC stems and QMD diagnostic, and its RESULT is not on the host, so neither its verdict nor its numbers is cited.
