< PREREG28 split the anchor by size (1.265 below 25 cm, 0.030 at and above) and PREREG28b kept 0.111 for large trees. Both passed every gate on screened qc_c fold B (pooled ratios 0.875 and 0.883), and under the preregistered choice rule the TOPHT difference (+11.64% against +11.97%, 0.33 points) fell under the 0.5 point threshold, so PREREG28b was named the QC candidate, at a TOPHT cost from +6.29% to +11.97%. PREREG33 reassigned the anchor from current DBH each year and kept every benchmark gate (TOPHT +11.14%).
