< PREREG37 asked what in the 14.1 height increment produces that size pattern, and found that the pattern is not a property of the increment. The PREREG23 helper, reused unchanged by PREREG28 and PREREG28b, read the run frames where TREE is a row index, the defect PREREG36 found for QC C2. Under MAGPlot field tags (737 fold B records against 301 by row index), observed over unanchored predicted increment is 1.169 pooled and 0.943 (0.643 to 1.235) at 25 cm and over, against 0.271 by row index, and the size contrast S is 1.265 against a preregistered threshold of 3.376. On field tags a single QC_AFAC near 1.17 fits, not 0.111. A weaker real size structure remains under field tags, which the H1 rule attributes to the height term, and the unanchored equation still reaches only 0.62 to 0.81 of ESI at age 50 from a seedling start. PREREG37 changed no frozen result. These notes no longer treat p28b_small as the 14.2 QC candidate, because its fit rests on row index pairs (PREREG37). The PREREG33 reassignment, which was never cleared, rests on the same pairs, and the QC anchor awaits a field tag refit. The same evidence bears on the shipped 0.111.
