< PREREG31 ran the Bakuzis QC grid for p28b_small and did not clear it, with four new site ordering flags and worse margins on Reineke (1.496 against 1.266) and basal area ordering (14 inversions against 13). The reference is not a credible long run projection, since under 14.1 every seeded tree keeps 0.111 for 100 years and top height at age 50 is 0.26 to 0.80 of ESI. PREREG33 failed the same grid (Reineke 1.412 against 1.266). Both grids tested anchors fitted on row index pairs (PREREG37), so they bound what those anchors do and say nothing yet about a field tag anchor.
---
> PREREG31 ran the Bakuzis QC grid for p28b_small and did not clear it, with four new site ordering flags and worse margins on Reineke (1.496 against 1.266) and basal area ordering (14 inversions against 13). The reference is not a credible long run projection, since under 14.1 every seeded tree keeps 0.111 for 100 years and top height at age 50 is 0.26 to 0.80 of ESI. PREREG33 failed the same grid (Reineke 1.412 against 1.266). Both grids tested anchors fitted on row index pairs (PREREG37). PREREG41 ran the same grid for the field tag anchor 1.242 against the frozen 14.1 trajectories and did not clear it either: three new basal area site ordering flags and a Reineke margin of 1.490 against 1.266, the same pattern as p28b_small. The margins are small and appear tied to the seedling start (stems rise from 1,000 to about 2,800 ha⁻¹ through ingrowth before any self thinning) and to the 2.5 m span of the QC ESI levels, but the rule was fixed before the grid was run and is not waived.
